From 03544e0b8db814b01030d8f3fa473531fe6fb0a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 19:11:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 08-05 WCAG-AA contrast gate (gtest + pair
 tables, D-07)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch slot 0114. Lands the chromium-side half of D-07's two-layer contrast
gate: contrast pair tables in phlink_palette.{h,cc} and a gtest
(phlink_color_contrast_unittests.cc) that walks each pair for both
ColorMode::kLight and ColorMode::kDark and asserts the WCAG 2.2 ratio via
color_utils::GetContrastRatio.

NormalText table (≥4.5:1) covers the 7 default-theme pairs verified in
.planning/sketches/phase-08/stitch-output.md §2.3 — Text/Canvas, Text/Surface,
Text/Card, Text/SurfaceAlt, TextMuted/Canvas, TextMuted/Surface, OnAccent/Accent
(the latter pinning the never-white invariant for both modes).

NonText table is intentionally size 0: stitch-output.md §2.3 does not gate
hairlines (they are decorative dividers, outside WCAG SC 1.4.11 scope), and
the (Accent, Canvas) Light pair is already mitigated by 2px stroke + check
icon (semantic redundancy). The structural slot is preserved so future
non-text UI affordances can be gated without a new gtest file.

Tests pass: 4 new + 11 prior PhlinkColor* = 15/15 SUCCESS.

Refs: APPR-05, D-07, D-12.
